WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.470
Speaker 1: Well, this you have to see to believe
or maybe not.

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:09.370
Donald Trump wants you and me taxpayers to
pay for his bogus special master.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.660
That never should have even been granted.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.690
So let's back up and I'll tell you what's
going on.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:21.699
Business Insider Headline Trump wants to split
the cost of the special master with the government,

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:24.609
but the DOJ wants him to pay for it.

00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:30.369
A judge granted Trump's request for a special
master, but the DOJ has appealed the decision.

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:35.010
Now, remember, Judge Eileen Cannon granted
Trump's request for a special master.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:40.660
A special master would take control of all
the documents seized from Trump's Mar a Lago,

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:45.660
would review them, and would see, are there
documents here that shouldn't be part of the

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:49.080
FBI investigation because they are in some
way privileged?

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.980
Are there documents here that shouldn't be
part of the investigation?

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:56.460
Maybe because they contain medical information
or whatever the case may be.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.030
That granting of a special master has been
found by legal experts who have weighed in

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:05.550
to be absolutely absurd and raises major questions
about Judge Eileen Cannon.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.920
Fine, but then we get to the question of who's
going to pay for this.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:15.910
A new court filing shows the two sides disagree
over who should pay for the special master.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:22.200
The government said Trump as the party requesting
the special master should bear the cost.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:29.810
But Trump wants the government to split it
with him, even though the DOJ does not agree.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:34.480
The filing also outlined disagreements between
the government and Trump's legal team regarding

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.960
how the entire special master process would
unfold.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:43.780
No surprise there, Trump's team proposed to
split evenly the professional fees and expenses

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.890
of the Special Master and any professionals,
support staff and expert consultants engaged

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.510
at the master's request.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.770
But the Justice Department has already started
reviewing the seized materials, doesn't want

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.770
a special master appointed and disagreed.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:03.760
The Government's position is that as the party
requesting, the Special Master Plaintiff should

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:09.780
bear the additional expense of the Special
Master's work.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:16.390
This actually could be so hypothetical if
Judge Eileen Cannon is coming around to the

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:20.700
fact that her decision to grant the Special
Master was the wrong decision.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.990
If she's coming around to that, this could
be a way to get out because we know Trump

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:29.400
doesn't pay for stuff and the decision could
be made.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.520
You pay for all of it or there is no special
master.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.700
That would be one thing that to look at that
would be interesting.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:41.940
But the whole premise of Trump's argument
and the judge ruling with him is that his

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.599
documents must be protected and sorted through.

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:51.170
The government doesn't have such a concern
if the government believes that they were

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:56.660
authorized to obtain the documents, that everything
was done on the up and up, all of those things.

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:03.880
And and indeed, remember that classified and
top secret documents, those aren't Trump's

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:04.880
documents.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.190
Those are government documents.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:11.580
If Trump wants to make the case they are his
documents and they shouldn't be released and

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.340
all of these different things, it should be
him.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:17.411
It should be he who actually ends up paying
for it.

00:03:17.411 --> 00:03:20.440
And we don't know if that's actually the direction
it's going to go.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:27.750
It doesn't make sense that Trump gets to dictate
to the government what of its own documents.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:33.560
Because remember, as William Barr has said
this, who else has said so many Republicans

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.360
have now said, these aren't Trump's documents.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.709
These are government documents.

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:40.600
These are the people's documents, for lack
of a better term.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.790
It doesn't make sense that Trump gets to tell
the government what they need to do with their

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.290
own documents, and then they also pay for
that.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.460
It is Trump who has to get to do that.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.440
He wants the special master.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.640
He should have to pay for it.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.810
It doesn't make sense to keep deferring to
him in this way.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.819
Now what's the strategy?

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:59.380
The strategy is just to delay.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.989
That's the strategy and it's a well known
legal strategy.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:10.670
You often it applies often in criminal trials
where most criminal defense attorneys will

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:14.830
tell you the longer we can delay, the better
for everybody.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:21.449
Number one, and this is I sort of say this
tongue in cheek, but also not the more motions

00:04:21.449 --> 00:04:26.229
to delay that a lawyer can file and succeed
with.

00:04:26.229 --> 00:04:31.300
The more the lawyer gets to bill, all else
being equal and continue extending, extending,

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.360
extending and listen.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.919
At the end of the day, yeah.

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:34.919
Lawyers want to make money.

00:04:34.919 --> 00:04:37.240
Speaker 4: Oh, the bonus show where you want
to make money?

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.439
Speaker 1: Yeah, sometimes people want to
make money, but that's not to suggest lawyers

00:04:40.439 --> 00:04:42.210
would unethically do that.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:46.370
There's also the legal explanation which lawyers
have told me, which is the longer you can

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:48.669
delay a criminal case.

00:04:48.669 --> 00:04:50.560
Witnesses might die.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:54.810
Witnesses recollection becomes less accurate.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.740
Documents might be lost, the evidence might
be misplaced.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:04.240
And it, generally speaking, favors defendants
to delay, delay, delay in criminal trials.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.509
Laws might change.

00:05:05.509 --> 00:05:07.409
This applies more to like white collar.

00:05:07.409 --> 00:05:11.309
And even though, generally speaking, the way
you are prosecuted is based on what the law

00:05:11.309 --> 00:05:12.490
was at the time.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:16.220
It's still not going to hurt you if the law
changes in a way that is fair.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:17.490
All these different things can happen.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.889
So that's the strategy here.

00:05:19.889 --> 00:05:21.659
DeLay as much as possible, period.

00:05:21.659 --> 00:05:23.430
And it's like a kid trying to delay bedtime.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:27.789
Well, you know, I need to use the bathroom
and I'm getting thirsty and.

00:05:27.789 --> 00:05:28.879
Oh, I don't know.

00:05:28.879 --> 00:05:31.029
I need to check what's my lunch tomorrow?

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:32.029
And now I'm hungry.

00:05:32.029 --> 00:05:33.029
And then.

00:05:33.029 --> 00:05:34.719
Oh, well, I got to brush my teeth again.

00:05:34.719 --> 00:05:37.309
It's the same type of thing.

00:05:37.309 --> 00:05:40.819
And now Trump wants you to pay for it and
hopefully that is rejected.

